"""S55 conservative provisional entry budgets from existing sealed evidence."""
from pathlib import Path
import hashlib,json
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];D=R/'inplace'
sha=lambda p:hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()
source=D/'S46-TEN-BOUND.json';bound=json.loads(source.read_text());sha_before=sha(source)
metrics={'load':'load_ns','writeback':'writeback_ns','guards':'guards_ns','unloader_init':'unloader_init_ns','program_lookup':'program_lookup_ns','binding':'binding_ns','result':'result_ns','native':'native_ns'}
rows=[];seals={str(source):sha_before,str(Path(__file__)):sha(Path(__file__))}
for row in bound['rows']:
 name=row['function'];program=row['program'];selection=D/'s43-selection-full33-v1'/program/'complete.json';seals[str(selection)]=sha(selection)
 prior=json.loads(selection.read_text());assert prior['complete']
 old=next(r for r in prior['region_times'] if r['function']==name);py=old['python_us']
 passes=[]
 for label in ('s46-ten-components-v7','s46-ten-components-v8'):
  path=D/label/'complete.json';seals[str(path)]=sha(path);d=json.loads(path.read_text());r=next(x for x in d['rows'] if x['function']==name);m=r['mean_exclusive_us']
  current={k:m[v] for k,v in metrics.items()};current['observer_bookkeeping']=m['bookkeeping_ns'];current['residual']=r['mean_complete_us']-sum(current.values())
  estimate={k:(0.0 if k in ('load','writeback','observer_bookkeeping') else v) for k,v in current.items()}
  passes.append({'label':label,'current':current,'observed_complete':r['mean_complete_us'],'estimated':estimate,'estimated_complete':sum(estimate.values()),'load_attempt_counts':sorted({a['phase_entries']['load_ns'] for a in r['attempts']}),'guard_attempt_counts':sorted({a['phase_entries']['guards_ns'] for a in r['attempts']}),'lookup_scope_counts':sorted({a['phase_entries']['program_lookup_ns'] for a in r['attempts']}),'retained_named':{k.removesuffix('_ns'):v for k,v in m.items() if k not in ('load_ns','writeback_ns','bookkeeping_ns')}})
 largest=max(passes[0]['retained_named'],key=lambda k:sum(p['retained_named'][k] for p in passes))
 rows.append({'function':name,'python_us':py,'prior_selection_compiled_us':old['compiled_us'],'passes':passes,'projected_below_python':all(p['estimated_complete']<py for p in passes),'largest_remaining_named_component':largest,'remaining_work':'Step2/3 demand-based guard/result-owner runtime; Step4b alone is insufficient','revised_first_touch_cost':'unknown; no measured prototype'})
assert all(sha(Path(p))==v for p,v in seals.items())
assert not any(r['projected_below_python'] for r in rows)
result={'complete':True,'model_only':True,'source_sha256':seals,'assumption':'Optimistically remove measured load, writeback and observer bookkeeping; retain every other observed exclusive component, including timers. This is a conservative provisional projection of conversion-only DESIGN93, not a measured speedup, lower bound, or a prediction for an unbuilt demand-based runtime. A future lazy design has unmeasured costs.','rows':rows,'projected_winners':0,'request':'S55.3: steer the next demand-based entry/result-owner prototype and budget before Step2/3 activation; initial conversion-only design is insufficient.'}
(D/'S55-ENTRY-BUDGET.json').write_text(json.dumps(result,indent=2))
def interval(values):return '–'.join(f'{v:.2f}' for v in (min(values),max(values)))
text=['# S55 per-region entry budget and steering request','','No region projects below its recorded Python time in the conservative provisional conversion-only model. This is the S55.3 request boundary; product edits for Steps2/3 have not begun. A read/store-only design cannot be accepted on this table.','','The model grants zero cost to both measured load and write-back, and excludes observer bookkeeping. All other measured components are retained unchanged. These are estimates to be confirmed, not a speedup, a mathematical lower bound or a performance prediction for an unbuilt lazy runtime. Timers remain inside the retained components; both source-identical passes overlapped peer correctness. Python times are the prior normal selection context, so comparison is a design budget check rather than a new deployment verdict.','','## Current components (us per observed replay)','','Each range is min–max of the two pass means. Native is dispatcher/body/boxing, not isolated machine work. Residual names all remaining exclusive phases in S46-TEN-BOUND.md.','','| Region | Python | Load | WB | Guards | Unloader init | Lookup | Binding | Result | Native | Observer bookkeeping | Residual |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
keys=(*metrics,'observer_bookkeeping','residual')
for row in rows:text.append('| '+row['function']+f" | {row['python_us']:.2f} | "+' | '.join(interval([p['current'][k] for p in row['passes']]) for k in keys)+' |')
text+=['','## Provisional projected components (us)','','Load/WB/observer are estimated at0. Every other entry below is explicitly unchanged from current cost; no unsupported discount is taken for moving code to C.','','| Region | Load | WB | Guards | Unloader init | Lookup | Binding | Result | Native | Residual | Complete estimate | Below Python | Largest named remainder |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|---|']
for row in rows:
 text.append('| '+row['function']+' | '+' | '.join(interval([p['estimated'][k] for p in row['passes']]) for k in (*metrics,'residual'))+' | '+interval([p['estimated_complete'] for p in row['passes']])+' | No | '+row['largest_remaining_named_component']+' |')
text+=['','## What needs to change','','The next architecture must validate object layout, exact kinds and binding dependencies at first touch on the executed native path, with per-interval deduplication. It must not walk every reachable object just to discover a numeric field or to copy the whole loader map into an _Unloader. Returned original objects need a demand-built handle-to-owner map; fresh outputs need conversion only for the returned graph. Live numeric/topology reads must be guarded when accessed. A class/object version cache is not assumed sound: it needs a proven invalidation mechanism, and no raw cached address survives a call. Callback-free dict/field probes must refuse possible user comparison/descriptor hooks rather than invoke them under borrowed state. The initial full-graph C walk in DESIGN93 is therefore superseded for the intended performance architecture.','','Program lookup is not merely a dictionary access. Source in heap.py::attempt tries latest guards/load and can then walk retained variants, checking cache membership/guards and attempting load before finding the selected specialization. Timed scopes exclude the nested load/guard time but retain resolver work, repeated branches and instrumentation. The actual counts below explain a structural difference from the trivial scalar/single-variant path; they do not causally attribute every microsecond. DeviceTask.fn has one load attempt yet9us lookup, so repeated variants alone do not explain all of other.','','| Region | Load/guard attempts per call v7 | v8 | Lookup scoped entries v7/v8 |','|---|---|---|---|']
for row in rows:
 a,b=row['passes'];text.append(f"| {row['function']} | {a['load_attempt_counts']} / {a['guard_attempt_counts']} | {b['load_attempt_counts']} / {b['guard_attempt_counts']} | {a['lookup_scope_counts']} / {b['lookup_scope_counts']} |")
text+=['','Use a guarded shallow call/dependency decision tree to choose retained variants without speculative full-graph loads. A live nested discriminator is inspected only with exact callback-free layout proof. A first-touch miss before effects declines; a miss after speculative stores rolls back; after a committed interpreter-fallback segment it must deopt from a continuation rather than replay earlier effects. This is missing runtime/compiler work, not a reason to skip target regions.','','Step4b only addresses the remaining boundary after demand-based work; its roughly2us measured scale cannot remove these retained tens/hundreds of microseconds. For every row, the largest remainder above therefore needs the Step2/3 entry/result-owner rework, not a claim that vectorcall will make it deploy. The revised lazy runtime has no measured per-touch budget yet; no region is declared projected-profitable on an invented C cost.','','## Steering request','','Per S55.3, do not activate the conversion-only design. Request steering on the next bounded item: build an independently reviewed, callback-free demand-based entry/result-owner prototype (first-touch layout/kind/binding checks, per-interval owner map, shallow retained-variant selector), establish its cost and exact fallback/observer behavior on the existing ten target inputs, and then rewrite the Step2/3 projections before activating direct payload access. No further ten-region component recorder pass is requested. The shared owner must also fix original method-source binding (CO_METHOD) before8of10 target summaries can authorize consumption; six executed positive method queries and the source comparison are in REQUESTS.md.','','This is an explicit incomplete-work request, not DONE. Direct reads/stores, S53 buffer-member runtime/SOR acceptance, Step4b and final kernel/selection acceptance remain open. Independent preparatory tests/design and the conservative shared-layer merge do not close them.']
(D/'S55-ENTRY-BUDGET.md').write_text('\n'.join(text)+'\n',encoding='utf8')
print('Verified ten rows; conversion-only provisional projected winners: 0')
for row in rows:print(row['function'],'Python',round(row['python_us'],3),'estimate',interval([p['estimated_complete'] for p in row['passes']]))
